From: Jihong Min <hurryman2212@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: keep NPU RRO data on its original RX queue

RRO 3.0 data queues normally defer completed A-MSDUs to the indicator
queue NAPI.  The Airoha NPU uses the same RRO queue flags, but completes
those packets through the original data queue and does not provide the
corresponding indicator activity.

Keep NPU-owned RRO data on its original RX queue.  Otherwise the packets
can remain queued until unrelated indicator activity occurs, severely
reducing receive throughput on 6 GHz EHT320 links.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6
Signed-off-by: Jihong Min <hurryman2212@gmail.com>
---
 mac80211.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -922,7 +922,8 @@ static void mt76_rx_release_amsdu(struct
 	/* RRO 3.0 data queue skbs are processed and completed in the context
 	 * of the indicator queue NAPI, which only polls its own skb list
 	 */
-	if (mt76_queue_is_wed_rro_data(rxq) && dev->hwrro_mode == MT76_HWRRO_V3)
+	if (!mt76_npu_device_active(dev) &&
+	    mt76_queue_is_wed_rro_data(rxq) && dev->hwrro_mode == MT76_HWRRO_V3)
 		q = MT_RXQ_RRO_IND;
 
 	__skb_queue_tail(&dev->rx_skb[q], skb);
